st in base and only exists on one side: take that side\n- If doc existed in base and was deleted on one side but unchanged on other: take deletion\n- If doc existed in base and was deleted on one side but modified on other: conflict? Hmm, the spec doesn't specify this. Let me think...\n\nActually, the spec says for each document that changed on either branch, we do field-level merge. So if a document was deleted on one branch and modified on another, that's a document-level conflict? Or should I treat deletion as \"all fields were removed\"?\n\nI think the simplest interpretation: if a document is deleted on one branch and modified on another, that's a conflict. If deleted on both, it's deleted. If deleted on one and unchanged on the other, take the deletion.\n\nBut what about \"unchanged\"? If the doc on the other branch is the same as the base, it's unchanged. If it's different, it's modified.\n\nLet me handle it like this:\n- Doc not in base, only on ours: we created it, take ours\n- Doc not in base, only on theirs: they created it, take theirs\n- Doc not in base, on both: both created independently, need deep merge\n- Doc in base, not on ours, not on theirs: both deleted, no conflict\n- Doc in base, not on ours (deleted), on theirs same as base: take deletion\n- Doc in base, not on ours (deleted), on theirs different from base: conflict (we deleted, they modified)\n- Doc in base, on ours same as base, not on theirs (deleted): take deletion\n- Doc in base, on ours different from base, not on theirs (deleted): conflict (we modified, they deleted)\n- Doc in base, on ours same as base, on theirs same as base: no change\n- Doc in base, on ours different, on theirs same: take ours\n- Doc in base, on ours same, on theirs different: take theirs\n- Doc in base, on ours different, on theirs different: need deep merge\n\nFor the \"conflict\" cases with delete vs modify, I'll report a conflict at the document level with path \"\" or the document ID.\n\nHmm, but the Conflict